  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="af57cf1b-3c54-54f1-a0c1-fbf612c3e37b" activityNameId="0790f3d6-e2c8-5d02-a885-e52a3de23b96" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Enamelling</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Enamelling
Enamel is a glass of a particular chemical composition and physical nature determined for the surface protection of metal.;
Synonyms: porcelain enamel; 
UUID: 75f47ffd-f134-32e9-ac23-0111ef6614fb
The basic inventory is split up into the major process stages degreasing, corroding, cleaning and firing as well as an inventory for the materials used for enamelling. All stages of enamelling are summed up not including the metal sheets treated. Data for infrastructure and land are estimated roughly with data for a metal coating plant.
Location: The inventory has been elaborated for the European situation based on data investigated in Germany.
Technology: Single layer enamelling process. Powder coating technology. 600g enamel per m2 of steel metal sheet. Specifications of steel not known.
Time period: Time of data collection.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature review, data provided by producers. 
Extrapolations: Study for Germany used as a basis for the assessment of the European average.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_75f47ffd-f134-32e9-ac23-0111ef6614fb.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
